What is a Cooling Distribution Unit?
Cooling Distribution Units (CDUs) serve as the circulatory system for liquid cooling architectures in data centers and other high-performance computing environments. These sophisticated systems precisely regulate coolant flow rates, maintain optimal temperature thresholds, and filter impurities—protecting sensitive electronics while maximizing thermal efficiency. Unlike conventional air cooling, CDUs enable higher density deployments by channeling heat away from components via liquid pathways, whether through air-to-liquid or liquid-to-liquid heat exchange configurations.
